[
 {
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 0.0
 },
 {
  "text": "As recently as six thousand years ago, the Sahara was green.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 0.0,
  "end": 2.312,
  "chunk": 0,
  "pause_after": 0.343
 },
 {
  "text": "Grass.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 2.656,
  "end": 2.933,
  "chunk": 1
 },
 {
  "text": "Lakes.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 2.933,
  "end": 3.211,
  "chunk": 1
 },
 {
  "text": "Rivers.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 3.211,
  "end": 3.489,
  "chunk": 1,
  "pause_after": 0.318
 },
 {
  "text": "Herds of animals, where today there is only sand.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 3.807,
  "end": 6.192,
  "chunk": 2
 },
 {
  "text": "It wasn't magic.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 6.192,
  "end": 6.987,
  "chunk": 2,
  "pause_after": 0.213
 },
 {
  "text": "Slow wobbles in Earth's orbit shifted the monsoon, and the rains moved north.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 7.2,
  "end": 10.771,
  "chunk": 3,
  "pause_after": 0.208
 },
 {
  "text": "Then, around five thousand years ago, the rains left.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 10.979,
  "end": 13.518,
  "chunk": 4
 },
 {
  "text": "Some studies say it happened fast.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 13.518,
  "end": 15.211,
  "chunk": 4,
  "pause_after": 0.567
 },
 {
  "text": "Now imagine they came back.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 15.778,
  "end": 16.713,
  "chunk": 5,
  "pause_after": 1.256
 },
 {
  "text": "Not just to the Sahara.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 17.969,
  "end": 18.941,
  "chunk": 6
 },
 {
  "text": "To every desert on Earth.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 18.941,
  "end": 19.912,
  "chunk": 6
 },
 {
  "text": "All of them, covered in forest.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 19.912,
  "end": 21.078,
  "chunk": 6,
  "pause_after": 0.227
 },
 {
  "text": "What would that do to the planet?",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 21.305,
  "end": 22.396,
  "chunk": 7,
  "pause_after": 0.625
 },
 {
  "text": "Let's find out.",
  "section": "THE GREEN SAHARA",
  "start": 23.022,
  "end": 23.76,
  "chunk": 8,
  "pause_after": 0.758
 },
 {
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 24.519
 },
 {
  "text": "First, the rules.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 24.519,
  "end": 25.374,
  "chunk": 9,
  "pause_after": 0.596
 },
 {
  "text": "Drylands cover about forty percent of the land outside Antarctica.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 25.969,
  "end": 29.374,
  "chunk": 10,
  "pause_after": 0.389
 },
 {
  "text": "The driest of them, the true deserts, cover roughly a sixth.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 29.763,
  "end": 32.214,
  "chunk": 11,
  "pause_after": 0.232
 },
 {
  "text": "In our story, every hot desert turns green with real forest, slowly, over decades.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 32.445,
  "end": 36.293,
  "chunk": 12,
  "pause_after": 0.268
 },
 {
  "text": "The polar deserts stay as they are.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 36.56,
  "end": 37.829,
  "chunk": 13
 },
 {
  "text": "Ice stays ice.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 37.829,
  "end": 38.373,
  "chunk": 13,
  "pause_after": 0.24
 },
 {
  "text": "And we won't explain where the rain comes from.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 38.613,
  "end": 40.425,
  "chunk": 14
 },
 {
  "text": "It simply arrives.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 40.425,
  "end": 41.029,
  "chunk": 14,
  "pause_after": 0.341
 },
 {
  "text": "The interesting question is what happens next.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 41.369,
  "end": 42.863,
  "chunk": 15,
  "pause_after": 0.321
 },
 {
  "text": "Start with the one thing every forest needs.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 43.183,
  "end": 45.297,
  "chunk": 16
 },
 {
  "text": "Water.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 45.297,
  "end": 45.562,
  "chunk": 16,
  "pause_after": 0.891
 },
 {
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 46.453
 },
 {
  "text": "A large tree can pull hundreds of litres of water out of the ground in a single day, and release it into the air.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 46.453,
  "end": 51.243,
  "chunk": 17,
  "pause_after": 0.35
 },
 {
  "text": "Now multiply that by billions of trees.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 51.593,
  "end": 53.39,
  "chunk": 18,
  "pause_after": 0.269
 },
 {
  "text": "In the Amazon, some research suggests about half the rain comes from the trees themselves.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 53.66,
  "end": 57.061,
  "chunk": 19,
  "pause_after": 0.3
 },
 {
  "text": "The forest waters itself.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 57.36,
  "end": 58.183,
  "chunk": 20
 },
 {
  "text": "That's the good news.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 58.183,
  "end": 59.006,
  "chunk": 20,
  "pause_after": 0.375
 },
 {
  "text": "Once a forest is established, it makes its own weather.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 59.381,
  "end": 61.268,
  "chunk": 21
 },
 {
  "text": "The bad news is the beginning.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 61.268,
  "end": 62.4,
  "chunk": 21,
  "pause_after": 0.254
 },
 {
  "text": "Young trees in dry ground die easily.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 62.654,
  "end": 64.071,
  "chunk": 22,
  "pause_after": 0.316
 },
 {
  "text": "That's why many real attempts to green a desert have hit the same wall.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 64.386,
  "end": 67.273,
  "chunk": 23,
  "pause_after": 0.36
 },
 {
  "text": "And there's a second wall, right under the trees' feet.",
  "section": "THE WATER",
  "start": 67.633,
  "end": 69.723,
  "chunk": 24,
  "pause_after": 0.854
 },
 {
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 70.577
 },
 {
  "text": "Forests need soil, and desert soil is thin, dry and poor.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 70.577,
  "end": 73.387,
  "chunk": 25,
  "pause_after": 0.292
 },
 {
  "text": "Soil forms painfully slowly.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 73.679,
  "end": 75.031,
  "chunk": 26,
  "pause_after": 0.447
 },
 {
  "text": "Depending on the climate, one inch of fertile topsoil can take hundreds of years to form, and in some places up to a thousand.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 75.478,
  "end": 80.07,
  "chunk": 27,
  "pause_after": 0.209
 },
 {
  "text": "So in our story, the forests wouldn't grow in a day.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 80.278,
  "end": 82.1,
  "chunk": 28,
  "pause_after": 0.368
 },
 {
  "text": "They would have to build their own ground first.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 82.468,
  "end": 84.145,
  "chunk": 29
 },
 {
  "text": "Fallen leaves.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 84.145,
  "end": 84.518,
  "chunk": 29,
  "pause_after": 0.393
 },
 {
  "text": "Roots.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 84.91,
  "end": 85.253,
  "chunk": 30
 },
 {
  "text": "Fungi.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 85.253,
  "end": 85.595,
  "chunk": 30
 },
 {
  "text": "Insects.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 85.595,
  "end": 85.937,
  "chunk": 30,
  "pause_after": 0.353
 },
 {
  "text": "Soil is something a forest slowly makes for itself.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 86.29,
  "end": 88.579,
  "chunk": 31
 },
 {
  "text": "It's a slow start.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 88.579,
  "end": 89.596,
  "chunk": 31,
  "pause_after": 0.695
 },
 {
  "text": "But once it gets going, it feeds itself.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 90.291,
  "end": 91.989,
  "chunk": 32,
  "pause_after": 0.385
 },
 {
  "text": "And once the forest starts breathing out water, the sky begins to change.",
  "section": "THE SOIL",
  "start": 92.373,
  "end": 95.103,
  "chunk": 33,
  "pause_after": 1.096
 },
 {
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 96.199
 },
 {
  "text": "Forests don't only drink.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 96.199,
  "end": 97.349,
  "chunk": 34,
  "pause_after": 0.431
 },
 {
  "text": "They send water up into the air.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 97.78,
  "end": 98.872,
  "chunk": 35,
  "pause_after": 0.342
 },
 {
  "text": "Winds carry that vapour for hundreds, even thousands, of kilometres.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 99.214,
  "end": 101.881,
  "chunk": 36,
  "pause_after": 0.381
 },
 {
  "text": "Scientists call these invisible streams flying rivers.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 102.262,
  "end": 104.876,
  "chunk": 37,
  "pause_after": 0.285
 },
 {
  "text": "A green Sahara could shift the winds and the monsoon rains across Africa, and beyond.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 105.16,
  "end": 109.386,
  "chunk": 38,
  "pause_after": 0.205
 },
 {
  "text": "Some regions might get wetter.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 109.591,
  "end": 111.061,
  "chunk": 39
 },
 {
  "text": "Others, drier.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 111.061,
  "end": 111.649,
  "chunk": 39
 },
 {
  "text": "Nobody can say for sure.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 111.649,
  "end": 113.118,
  "chunk": 39,
  "pause_after": 0.592
 },
 {
  "text": "But there's one effect we can already estimate.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 113.71,
  "end": 115.216,
  "chunk": 40,
  "pause_after": 0.213
 },
 {
  "text": "And it lands on the other side of the Atlantic.",
  "section": "THE FLYING RIVERS",
  "start": 115.429,
  "end": 116.895,
  "chunk": 41,
  "pause_after": 0.806
 },
 {
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 117.7
 },
 {
  "text": "Every year, wind lifts dust from the Sahara and carries it across the ocean.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 117.7,
  "end": 120.675,
  "chunk": 42,
  "pause_after": 0.286
 },
 {
  "text": "About twenty-eight million tonnes of it fall on the Amazon.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 120.961,
  "end": 123.106,
  "chunk": 43,
  "pause_after": 0.218
 },
 {
  "text": "Inside that dust is phosphorus, a nutrient the rainforest soil badly needs.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 123.324,
  "end": 127.383,
  "chunk": 44,
  "pause_after": 0.321
 },
 {
  "text": "NASA satellite data suggest around twenty-two thousand tonnes arrive each year.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 127.704,
  "end": 131.576,
  "chunk": 45,
  "pause_after": 0.38
 },
 {
  "text": "Much of it comes from one place, the Bod\u00e9l\u00e9 Depression, the bed of an ancient lake.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 131.956,
  "end": 135.594,
  "chunk": 46,
  "pause_after": 0.261
 },
 {
  "text": "These numbers are estimates.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 135.855,
  "end": 136.998,
  "chunk": 47,
  "pause_after": 0.485
 },
 {
  "text": "Some years bring five times more than others, and not all the phosphorus is usable by plants.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 137.483,
  "end": 140.896,
  "chunk": 48,
  "pause_after": 0.789
 },
 {
  "text": "But the idea holds.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 141.686,
  "end": 142.662,
  "chunk": 49,
  "pause_after": 0.452
 },
 {
  "text": "The Amazon is partly fed by the Sahara.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 143.114,
  "end": 144.678,
  "chunk": 50,
  "pause_after": 0.251
 },
 {
  "text": "Green the Sahara, and that dust would likely slow or stop.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 144.929,
  "end": 147.414,
  "chunk": 51,
  "pause_after": 0.33
 },
 {
  "text": "A forest that grows in one desert could starve a forest on the other side of the world.",
  "section": "THE DUST",
  "start": 147.744,
  "end": 151.213,
  "chunk": 52,
  "pause_after": 0.931
 },
 {
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 152.143
 },
 {
  "text": "Forests are dark.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 152.143,
  "end": 152.897,
  "chunk": 53
 },
 {
  "text": "Sand is bright.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 152.897,
  "end": 153.65,
  "chunk": 53,
  "pause_after": 0.281
 },
 {
  "text": "Desert sand reflects roughly thirty to forty percent of sunlight back into space.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 153.931,
  "end": 157.184,
  "chunk": 54,
  "pause_after": 0.41
 },
 {
  "text": "A forest reflects only about eight to fifteen percent.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 157.594,
  "end": 159.368,
  "chunk": 55,
  "pause_after": 0.313
 },
 {
  "text": "Swap sand for forest, and the ground absorbs more sunlight.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 159.682,
  "end": 161.8,
  "chunk": 56,
  "pause_after": 0.349
 },
 {
  "text": "Trees also cool the air by releasing water vapour, a little like sweating.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 162.149,
  "end": 165.128,
  "chunk": 57,
  "pause_after": 0.398
 },
 {
  "text": "Which effect wins?",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 165.525,
  "end": 166.401,
  "chunk": 58,
  "pause_after": 0.675
 },
 {
  "text": "It depends on where, and scientists argue about it.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 167.076,
  "end": 169.186,
  "chunk": 59,
  "pause_after": 0.286
 },
 {
  "text": "What's clear is that you can't simply paint the planet green and expect it to cool.",
  "section": "THE HEAT",
  "start": 169.473,
  "end": 172.873,
  "chunk": 60,
  "pause_after": 0.708
 },
 {
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 173.581
 },
 {
  "text": "Of course, trees also pull carbon dioxide out of the air.",
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 173.581,
  "end": 175.816,
  "chunk": 61,
  "pause_after": 0.214
 },
 {
  "text": "New forests across a sixth of the world's land could lock away a great deal of carbon, if the trees survive and keep growing.",
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 176.03,
  "end": 180.845,
  "chunk": 62,
  "pause_after": 0.602
 },
 {
  "text": "But carbon stored in a forest can return to the air if it burns or dies.",
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 181.447,
  "end": 184.307,
  "chunk": 63,
  "pause_after": 0.275
 },
 {
  "text": "And forests in dry places burn.",
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 184.582,
  "end": 185.82,
  "chunk": 64,
  "pause_after": 0.2
 },
 {
  "text": "So the climate maths comes with a long list of ifs.",
  "section": "THE AIR",
  "start": 186.02,
  "end": 188.26,
  "chunk": 65,
  "pause_after": 0.897
 },
 {
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 189.157
 },
 {
  "text": "Is there a shortcut?",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 189.157,
  "end": 190.005,
  "chunk": 66,
  "pause_after": 0.505
 },
 {
  "text": "One surprising answer comes from a computer model.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 190.51,
  "end": 192.505,
  "chunk": 67,
  "pause_after": 0.335
 },
 {
  "text": "In twenty eighteen, scientists simulated covering a huge part of the Sahara with wind and solar farms.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 192.84,
  "end": 197.243,
  "chunk": 68,
  "pause_after": 0.255
 },
 {
  "text": "Dark panels absorb more sunlight than pale sand, and that warms the ground.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 197.498,
  "end": 200.613,
  "chunk": 69,
  "pause_after": 0.28
 },
 {
  "text": "Turbines stir the air.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 200.894,
  "end": 201.892,
  "chunk": 70,
  "pause_after": 0.573
 },
 {
  "text": "In the model, together they pushed the rainfall up.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 202.464,
  "end": 203.979,
  "chunk": 71,
  "pause_after": 0.303
 },
 {
  "text": "Across the Sahara, rain more than doubled.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 204.281,
  "end": 206.123,
  "chunk": 72,
  "pause_after": 0.219
 },
 {
  "text": "In the Sahel, the dry belt to the south, it rose by roughly two hundred to five hundred millimetres a year.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 206.342,
  "end": 211.207,
  "chunk": 73,
  "pause_after": 0.275
 },
 {
  "text": "More rain meant more plants, and more plants meant even more rain.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 211.483,
  "end": 214.455,
  "chunk": 74,
  "pause_after": 0.382
 },
 {
  "text": "A loop that feeds itself.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 214.837,
  "end": 215.761,
  "chunk": 75,
  "pause_after": 0.205
 },
 {
  "text": "It's a model, not a measurement, and the scale was enormous, about nine million square kilometres.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 215.966,
  "end": 219.715,
  "chunk": 76,
  "pause_after": 0.682
 },
 {
  "text": "But it shows something remarkable.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 220.397,
  "end": 221.503,
  "chunk": 77,
  "pause_after": 0.319
 },
 {
  "text": "Deserts and rain can talk to each other.",
  "section": "THE SOLAR WAY",
  "start": 221.822,
  "end": 223.253,
  "chunk": 78,
  "pause_after": 0.803
 },
 {
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 224.056
 },
 {
  "text": "Then there are the people.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 224.056,
  "end": 224.906,
  "chunk": 79,
  "pause_after": 0.39
 },
 {
  "text": "Deserts are hot and dry, but the lands around them aren't empty.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 225.296,
  "end": 228.24,
  "chunk": 80,
  "pause_after": 0.257
 },
 {
  "text": "About two point three billion people live in drylands, which include the semi-arid regions bordering deserts.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 228.498,
  "end": 233.87,
  "chunk": 81,
  "pause_after": 0.237
 },
 {
  "text": "That's roughly three in ten of all people on Earth.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 234.107,
  "end": 235.712,
  "chunk": 82,
  "pause_after": 0.317
 },
 {
  "text": "Greener land could bring more water, more grazing and more farms.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 236.029,
  "end": 238.505,
  "chunk": 83,
  "pause_after": 0.632
 },
 {
  "text": "But for nomadic herding peoples, whose way of life depends on open, dry land, a forest isn't automatically a gift.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 239.137,
  "end": 244.077,
  "chunk": 84,
  "pause_after": 0.379
 },
 {
  "text": "Some would gain.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 244.455,
  "end": 244.995,
  "chunk": 85
 },
 {
  "text": "Some would lose.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 244.995,
  "end": 245.535,
  "chunk": 85
 },
 {
  "text": "And so would the animals.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 245.535,
  "end": 246.434,
  "chunk": 85,
  "pause_after": 0.388
 },
 {
  "text": "Deserts aren't empty.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 246.822,
  "end": 247.683,
  "chunk": 86
 },
 {
  "text": "Plants that store water for years.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 247.683,
  "end": 249.405,
  "chunk": 86,
  "pause_after": 0.38
 },
 {
  "text": "Insects, reptiles and mammals built for heat and very little rain.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 249.785,
  "end": 252.77,
  "chunk": 87,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "They would lose their home.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 253.02,
  "end": 254.297,
  "chunk": 88
 },
 {
  "text": "A desert isn't a wasteland.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 254.297,
  "end": 255.573,
  "chunk": 88
 },
 {
  "text": "It's an ecosystem.",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 255.573,
  "end": 256.338,
  "chunk": 88,
  "pause_after": 0.278
 },
 {
  "text": "So has anyone actually tried to green one?",
  "section": "THE WINNERS AND THE LOSERS",
  "start": 256.617,
  "end": 258.526,
  "chunk": 89,
  "pause_after": 1.027
 },
 {
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 259.553
 },
 {
  "text": "Africa has.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 259.553,
  "end": 260.323,
  "chunk": 90,
  "pause_after": 0.467
 },
 {
  "text": "The Great Green Wall aims to restore one hundred million hectares across the Sahel by twenty thirty.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 260.789,
  "end": 264.601,
  "chunk": 91,
  "pause_after": 0.41
 },
 {
  "text": "It isn't really a wall.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 265.012,
  "end": 265.816,
  "chunk": 92,
  "pause_after": 0.406
 },
 {
  "text": "It's a patchwork of projects: trees, grasses and better farming, along a belt thousands of kilometres long.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 266.223,
  "end": 271.134,
  "chunk": 93,
  "pause_after": 0.41
 },
 {
  "text": "How far along is it?",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 271.544,
  "end": 272.437,
  "chunk": 94,
  "pause_after": 0.544
 },
 {
  "text": "The official count in twenty twenty put it at about four percent.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 272.981,
  "end": 275.889,
  "chunk": 95,
  "pause_after": 0.243
 },
 {
  "text": "Counting the wider region, about eighteen percent.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 276.132,
  "end": 277.77,
  "chunk": 96,
  "pause_after": 0.337
 },
 {
  "text": "To hit the target, the countries involved would need to restore about eight million hectares every single year.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 278.108,
  "end": 281.97,
  "chunk": 97,
  "pause_after": 0.385
 },
 {
  "text": "It's slow.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 282.355,
  "end": 282.93,
  "chunk": 98,
  "pause_after": 0.713
 },
 {
  "text": "But it has turned some dry land into land that can feed people.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 283.643,
  "end": 285.941,
  "chunk": 99,
  "pause_after": 0.219
 },
 {
  "text": "China tried something even bigger.",
  "section": "THE GREAT GREEN WALL",
  "start": 286.16,
  "end": 287.613,
  "chunk": 100,
  "pause_after": 0.899
 },
 {
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 288.512
 },
 {
  "text": "In nineteen seventy-eight, China began a huge tree-planting programme across its dry north, and it is still running.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 288.512,
  "end": 293.204,
  "chunk": 101,
  "pause_after": 0.365
 },
 {
  "text": "It helped hold some sand in place.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 293.569,
  "end": 295.19,
  "chunk": 102
 },
 {
  "text": "It also ran into limits.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 295.19,
  "end": 296.349,
  "chunk": 102,
  "pause_after": 0.239
 },
 {
  "text": "Critics say many of the planted trees died, and that too many were the same species.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 296.588,
  "end": 299.877,
  "chunk": 103,
  "pause_after": 0.273
 },
 {
  "text": "And the trees needed water.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 300.15,
  "end": 301.106,
  "chunk": 104,
  "pause_after": 0.414
 },
 {
  "text": "In some places, groundwater fell by as much as nineteen metres.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 301.52,
  "end": 303.96,
  "chunk": 105,
  "pause_after": 0.288
 },
 {
  "text": "More recently, some areas have tried solar panels with plants growing beneath them.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 304.249,
  "end": 307.416,
  "chunk": 106,
  "pause_after": 0.359
 },
 {
  "text": "Whether that works in the long run is still being tested.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 307.776,
  "end": 309.94,
  "chunk": 107,
  "pause_after": 0.228
 },
 {
  "text": "The lesson is simple.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 310.168,
  "end": 311.157,
  "chunk": 108,
  "pause_after": 0.583
 },
 {
  "text": "Green only lasts where the water does.",
  "section": "THE TREE BELT",
  "start": 311.74,
  "end": 313.133,
  "chunk": 109,
  "pause_after": 0.95
 },
 {
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 314.084
 },
 {
  "text": "So here's the strangest part.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 314.084,
  "end": 315.328,
  "chunk": 110
 },
 {
  "text": "Nature has already run this experiment.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 315.328,
  "end": 316.82,
  "chunk": 110,
  "pause_after": 0.416
 },
 {
  "text": "The Sahara turned green on its own, pushed by a wobble in Earth's orbit, and then it turned back.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 317.236,
  "end": 320.614,
  "chunk": 111,
  "pause_after": 0.277
 },
 {
  "text": "Mostly, that wasn't people.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 320.891,
  "end": 321.751,
  "chunk": 112
 },
 {
  "text": "It was physics.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 321.751,
  "end": 322.395,
  "chunk": 112,
  "pause_after": 0.229
 },
 {
  "text": "Which means a green desert isn't only a dream.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 322.624,
  "end": 324.485,
  "chunk": 113,
  "pause_after": 0.414
 },
 {
  "text": "It's a state the planet has been in before.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 324.899,
  "end": 326.688,
  "chunk": 114
 },
 {
  "text": "And a state it can leave.",
  "section": "THE REAL TWIST",
  "start": 326.688,
  "end": 327.882,
  "chunk": 114,
  "pause_after": 0.753
 },
 {
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 328.634
 },
 {
  "text": "So what if every desert turned green?",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 328.634,
  "end": 330.189,
  "chunk": 115,
  "pause_after": 0.587
 },
 {
  "text": "The Amazon might lose its dust.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 330.775,
  "end": 331.945,
  "chunk": 116,
  "pause_after": 0.382
 },
 {
  "text": "The winds and the rains would shift.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 332.327,
  "end": 333.399,
  "chunk": 117,
  "pause_after": 0.255
 },
 {
  "text": "The planet could store more carbon, and also absorb more sunlight.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 333.654,
  "end": 336.064,
  "chunk": 118,
  "pause_after": 0.253
 },
 {
  "text": "And the animals and people of the desert would lose their home.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 336.317,
  "end": 338.328,
  "chunk": 119,
  "pause_after": 0.257
 },
 {
  "text": "Maybe the lesson isn't how to remove deserts.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 338.586,
  "end": 340.244,
  "chunk": 120,
  "pause_after": 0.229
 },
 {
  "text": "It's that every landscape is a balance, and every balance has a price.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 340.472,
  "end": 343.612,
  "chunk": 121,
  "pause_after": 0.278
 },
 {
  "text": "Six thousand years ago, the Sahara was green.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 343.889,
  "end": 346.029,
  "chunk": 122
 },
 {
  "text": "The rains left.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 346.029,
  "end": 346.831,
  "chunk": 122,
  "pause_after": 1.296
 },
 {
  "text": "Would you bring them back?",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 348.127,
  "end": 349.003,
  "chunk": 123,
  "pause_after": 2.0
 }
]